           }\n                if (x+y+1 <= 2*n-d && str.charAt((int)(n-x+n-y-1)) != 'A') {\n                    long newarea2 = totalarea[(int)(n-x)][(int)(n-y)] - totalarea[(int)(n-x-1)][(int)(n-y)];\n                    for (Map.Entry<Long,Long> it : bp[x][y].entrySet()) {\n                        if (it.getKey() + newarea2 > m2) continue;\n                        bp[x+1][y].put(it.getKey() + newarea2, bp[x+1][y].getOrDefault(it.getKey() + newarea2, 0L) + it.getValue());\n                    }\n                }\n                if (x+y+1 <= d) dp[x][y].clear();\n                if (x+y+1 <= 2*n-d) bp[x][y].clear();\n            }\n        }\n        // Final combine\n        for (int x = 0; x <= n; x++) {\n            long y = d - x;\n            if (y < 0 || y > n) continue;\n            for (Map.Entry<Long,Long> it : dp[x][(int)y].entrySet()) {\n                long c = it.getKey();\n                long freq = it.getValue();\n                bestfreq += freq * bp[(int)(n-x)][(int)(n-y)].getOrDefault(m1 - c, 0L);\n                if (m1 != m2) bestfreq += freq * bp[(int)(n-x)][(int)(n-y)].getOrDefault(m2 - c, 0L);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(bestfreq);\n    }\n}\n\nBut note: In the original code, the ans array is 30x30 but only up to 20 used. We allocated 21x21. Also need to add L suffix to large numbers to avoid overflow at compile time. For numbers that fit in long, we can use L.\n\nAlso note that in the original, 'ans' is declared as long long ans[30][30]; and then assignments. In Java we declared ans as long[21][21]; and fill.\n\nOne more thing: In the original DP for (y < n) loop, the condition for backward move uses 'bp[x][y]' but after that, the same bp[x][y] is used in moves to x+1. In our code, we clear maps after processing x+1 moves, which is correct.\n\nEdge case: d may be > n? It can be up to 2n-1. The loops for x and y: x up to n, y up to n, but d can be larger; but the condition x+y+1 <= d ensures we only access when within bound. For backward, condition x+y+1 <= 2*n-d also ensures. So fine.\n\nAlso, the map keys are summed, may become large but fine.\n\nWe should ensure that when we getOrDefault, we use 0L.\n\nNow, produce final output with tags.<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long[][] ncr = new long[40][40];\n        long[][] ans = new long[21][21]; // 1-indexed up to 20\n\n        // Initialize ans array\n        ans[1][1]=0; ans[1][2]=1; ans[1][3]=0; ans[1][4]=1; ans[1][5]=0;\n        ans[1][6]=1; ans[1][7]=0; ans[1][8]=1; ans[1][9]=0; ans[1][10]=1;\n        ans[1][11]=0; ans[1][12]=1; ans[1][13]=0; ans[1][14]=1; ans[1][15]=0;\n        ans[1][16]=1; ans[1][17]=0; ans[1][18]=1; ans[1][19]=0; ans[1][20]=1;\n        ans[2][1]=3; ans[2][2]=0; ans[2][3]=2; ans[2][4]=3; ans[2][5]=1;\n        ans[2][6]=0; ans[2][7]=0; ans[2][8]=1; ans[2][9]=1; ans[2][10]=0;\n        ans[2][11]=0; ans[2][12]=1; ans[2][13]=1; ans[2][14]=0; ans[2][15]=0;\n        ans[2][16]=1; ans[2][17]=1; ans[2][18]=0; ans[2][19]=0; ans[2][20]=1;\n        ans[3][1]=8; ans[3][2]=20; ans[3][3]=0; ans[3][4]=15; ans[3][5]=16;\n        ans[3][6]=0; ans[3][7]=0; ans[3][8]=1; ans[3][9]=0; ans[3][10]=0;\n        ans[3][11]=0; ans[3][12]=1; ans[3][13]=0; ans[3][14]=0; ans[3][15]=0;\n        ans[3][16]=1; ans[3][17]=0; ans[3][18]=0; ans[3][19]=0; ans[3][20]=1;\n        ans[4][1]=15; ans[4][2]=75; ans[4][3]=175; ans[4][4]=0; ans[4][5]=4;\n        ans[4][6]=0; ans[4][7]=0; ans[4][8]=45; ans[4][9]=15; ans[4][10]=1;\n        ans[4][11]=1; ans[4][12]=0; ans[4][13]=0; ans[4][14]=0; ans[4][15]=0;\n        ans[4][16]=1; ans[4][17]=1; ans[4][18]=1; ans[4][19]=1; ans[4][20]=0;\n        ans[5][1]=24; ans[5][2]=189; ans[5][3]=784; ans[5][4]=1764; ans[5][5]=0;\n        ans[5][6]=0; ans[5][7]=60; ans[5][8]=95; ans[5][9]=200; ans[5][10]=1;\n        ans[5][11]=14; ans[5][12]=14; ans[5][13]=0; ans[5][14]=4; ans[5][15